# The Short S.23's control surfaces (src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a line is
# read): each a hinge line from its inboard or lower end to its other, in the
# model's body frame, metres from its origin - +x forward, +y starboard, +z
# down - then how far forward of the hinge the part reaches, how far aft, and
# how far either side of the hinge's plane; and first the JSBSim property
# whose value, in radians, is its deflection, with which way a positive value
# moves its trailing edge.
#
# Measured off the model's own sections (assets/models/short_s23.mesh), by
# slicing it where each surface ends: the ailerons between 62% and 93% of the
# wing's semispan, each hinge a quarter of the local chord forward of the
# trailing edge;
# the elevators from 0.8 m out to 4.3 m, hinged three tenths of the
# chord forward of the trailing edge;
# the rudder from 3.9 m above the origin to 7.0 m,
# hinged three tenths of the chord forward of the trailing edge.
# The sections each was measured from are above its lines.
#
# wing -12.08..-8.30 at 10.76 m, -10.92..-8.76 at 16.15 m
surface left-aileron    fcs/left-aileron-pos-rad   down  -11.137 -10.764 -2.798  -10.380 -16.146 -3.060  0.000 1.109 0.601
surface right-aileron   fcs/right-aileron-pos-rad  down  -11.137 10.764 -2.798  -10.380 16.146 -3.060  0.000 1.109 0.601
# tail -26.03..-18.28 at 0.80 m, -25.65..-24.31 at 4.30 m
surface left-elevator   fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -23.707 -0.800 -3.247  -25.245 -4.300 -3.300  0.000 2.693 0.386
surface right-elevator  fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -23.707 0.800 -3.247  -25.245 4.300 -3.300  0.000 2.693 0.386
# fin -26.44..-23.05 at -3.90 m, -26.03..-23.91 at -7.00 m
surface rudder          fcs/rudder-pos-rad         left  -25.426 0.000 -3.900  -25.394 0.000 -7.000  0.000 1.189 0.422
